      "traceTextDiagram": "Skill Execution Entry Point (runner.go)\n├── RunWithOptions() entry \u003c-- 1a\n│   ├── workspace.FromContext(ctx) \u003c-- 1b\n│   │   └── Extract workspace path \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/platform/workspace/context.go:22\n│   ├── switch on Distribution.Type \u003c-- 1c\n│   │   ├── case \"exec\": \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/runner/runner.go:85\n│   │   │   ├── Create execrunner.Runner \u003c-- 1d\n│   │   │   ├── buildSkillEnv(os.Environ(), ...) \u003c-- 1e\n│   │   │   │   └── Inherits parent env, session vars\n│   │   │   │       pass through automatically\n│   │   │   └── r.Run(ctx, input) \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/runner/runner.go:93\n│   │   │       └── → Trace 2: Exec Runtime\n│   │   └── case \"wasi\": \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/runner/runner.go:94\n│   │       ├── Create wasirunner.Runner \u003c-- 1f\n│   │       ├── buildSkillEnv(nil, ws, true) \u003c-- 1g\n│   │       │   └── Empty base, explicit session\n│   │       │       var propagation required\n│   │       └── r.Run(ctx, input) \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/runner/runner.go:102\n│   │           └── → Trace 3: WASI Runtime\n│   └── Return stdout, stderr, error",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nSkills in agentctl can be distributed as **native binaries** (exec) or **WebAssembly modules** (WASI). These two runtime types have fundamentally different execution models: native binaries inherit the parent process environment automatically, while WebAssembly runs in an **isolated sandbox** with no environment by default. The unified runner [1a] solves the problem of executing both types through a single interface while handling their different environment propagation needs.\n\nA critical requirement is **session tracking across AI coding tools**. When Claude Code, Cursor, or other tools invoke agentctl skills, those skills need to know which session they're running in to maintain lineage and context. The system must propagate session IDs like `AGENTCTL_SESSION_ID` and `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` from parent to child processes—but this propagation works differently for exec vs WASI.\n\n## Details\n\n### Unified Entry Point\n\n`RunWithOptions` [1a] is the main entry point that routes skill execution. It first extracts the workspace from the context [1b], then dispatches based on the manifest's distribution type [1c]. This single function handles both exec and WASI skills transparently.\n\n### Exec Runtime Path\n\nFor native binaries [1d], the runner calls `buildSkillEnv` with `os.Environ()` as the base [1e]. This means the child process **inherits all parent environment variables automatically**, including session tracking variables. The `propagateSessionVars` parameter is `false` because propagation happens implicitly through OS inheritance.\n\n### WASI Runtime Path\n\nFor WebAssembly modules [1f], the runner calls `buildSkillEnv` with `nil` as the base [1g]. WASI starts with an **empty environment** for security isolation. The `propagateSessionVars` parameter is `true`, which triggers explicit iteration through session variables (`AGENTCTL_SESSION_ID`, `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`, etc.) and adds them one-by-one to the WASI environment. Without this explicit propagation, WASI skills would have no session context.\n\n### Environment Builder\n\nThe `buildSkillEnv` function constructs the skill's environment. When `propagateSessionVars` is true, it loops through a predefined list of session tracking variables, reads each from the parent environment using `env.GetString`, and appends them to the child environment. This ensures consistent session lineage regardless of which AI tool invoked the skill.\n\n### Workspace Propagation\n\nBoth runtimes receive `AGENTCTL_WORKSPACE` in their environment, enabling skills to detect git repositories and project structure. The workspace is detected using a priority chain: context value → `AGENTCTL_WORKSPACE` env var → `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` → git markers."
    },
