          "lineContent": "job, duplicate, err := e.prepareSkillJob(ctx, manifest.Metadata.Name, input, false)",
          "title": "Prepare job record",
          "description": "Creates job entry in database with queued state"
        },
        {
          "id": "5c",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 318,
          "lineContent": "result, execErr := e.skillExecutor.Execute(ctx, execution.ExecuteOptions{",
          "title": "Execute via skill executor",
          "description": "Delegates to SkillExecutor interface (typically RunnerExecutor)"
        },
        {
          "id": "5d",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 284,
          "lineContent": "if err := e.persist.UpdateState(ctx, jobID, types.StateRunning, \"\", \"\"); err != nil {",
          "title": "Update job state to running",
          "description": "Persists state transition before execution"
        },
        {
          "id": "5e",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 246,
          "lineContent": "observability.Emit(ctx, eventBuilder.Error(runErr, duration))",
          "title": "Emit observability event",
          "description": "Records execution metrics and traces for monitoring"
        },
        {
          "id": "5f",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go",
          "lineNumber": 394,
          "lineContent": "if err := e.persist.UpdateState(stateCtx, jobID, types.StateOK, \"\", resultPath); err != nil {",
          "title": "Persist success state",
          "description": "Updates job state to OK with result path on successful completion"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Job Executor Orchestration\n├── RunSkill() entry \u003c-- 5a\n│   ├── prepareSkillJob() \u003c-- 5b\n│   │   ├── Create job record (ULID, queued state) \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:150\n│   │   ├── InsertJob() to persistence \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:171\n│   │   └── Write input.json to job directory \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:181\n│   └── executeSkill() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:189\n│       ├── startExecution() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:190\n│       │   └── UpdateState(StateRunning) \u003c-- 5d\n│       ├── runSkill() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:228\n│       │   └── skillExecutor.Execute() \u003c-- 5c\n│       │       └── runner.RunWithOptions() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:336\n│       │           └── [exec or WASI runtime]\n│       ├── observability.Emit() \u003c-- 5e\n│       └── handleSuccess() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:251\n│           ├── Unmarshal \u0026 validate envelope \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:367\n│           ├── Write result.json \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/jobs/executor/executor.go:386\n│           └── UpdateState(StateOK) \u003c-- 5f",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nSkills in agentctl need to run reliably with **full lifecycle tracking**—from submission through execution to completion. The job executor provides this orchestration layer, ensuring that every skill execution is:\n\n- **Persisted** with a unique job ID before execution begins\n- **State-tracked** through queued → running → ok/error transitions\n- **Observable** with metrics and traces for debugging\n- **Recoverable** with results written to disk for later retrieval\n\nWithout this layer, skill executions would be ephemeral—if a process crashes or the user disconnects, there's no way to know what happened or retrieve results. The executor solves this by treating each skill run as a **durable job** with persistent state.\n\n## Details\n\n### Job Preparation\n\nThe executor starts by creating a job record [5b] with a ULID identifier, computing an args hash for deduplication, and setting the initial state to `queued`. It writes the input JSON to a job-specific directory on disk, ensuring the execution context is preserved even if the process restarts.\n\n### Execution Orchestration\n\nThe `executeSkill()` method [at executor.go:189] coordinates the full lifecycle:\n\n1. **State transition to running** [5d]—updates the database before execution begins so monitoring systems can track in-flight jobs\n2. **Skill execution** [5c]—delegates to the `SkillExecutor` interface, which typically routes through `runner.RunWithOptions()` [at executor.go:336] to either the exec or WASI runtime\n3. **Observability emission** [5e]—records execution metrics, duration, and traces with enriched cloud metadata for debugging\n\n### Result Handling\n\nOn successful execution, `handleSuccess()` [at executor.go:251] validates the skill's envelope output, writes `result.json` to the job directory, and updates the database state to `ok` [5f]. The result path is stored in the database, allowing clients to retrieve outputs later.\n\n### Error Resilience\n\nThe executor uses **background contexts** for final state updates to ensure they complete even if the original request context was cancelled. This prevents jobs from getting stuck in \"running\" state when timeouts occur.\n\n### Integration Points\n\nThe executor is used by:\n- **CLI commands** for interactive skill runs\n- **Daemon service** for fast repeated executions\n- **Hook system** for lifecycle event-triggered skills\n- **Agent runtime** for autonomous skill orchestration"
    },
