      "id": "7",
      "title": "Daemon Service Fast Path",
      "description": "Daemon service - provides low-latency skill execution through persistent service with pre-warmed resources",
      "locations": [
        {
          "id": "7a",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 326,
          "lineContent": "func (s *Service) handleRun(ctx context.Context, params json.RawMessage) (*RunResult, error) {",
          "title": "Daemon run handler",
          "description": "Handles skill execution requests via Unix socket"
        },
        {
          "id": "7b",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 354,
          "lineContent": "stdout, stderr, err := runner.RunWithOptions(ctx, runner.RunOptions{",
          "title": "Execute via unified runner",
          "description": "Calls RunWithOptions directly for fast execution path"
        },
        {
          "id": "7c",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 345,
          "lineContent": "extraEnv := s.buildSkillEnv(p.Workspace)",
          "title": "Build daemon environment",
          "description": "Constructs environment with workspace and session propagation"
        },
        {
          "id": "7d",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 396,
          "lineContent": "for _, key := range []string{",
          "title": "Propagate session vars",
          "description": "Reads AGENTCTL_SESSION_ID, CLAUDE_SESSION_ID, etc. from daemon environment"
        },
        {
          "id": "7e",
          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go",
          "lineNumber": 400,
          "lineContent": "if v := os.Getenv(key); v != \"\" {",
          "title": "Read parent environment",
          "description": "Retrieves session variables from daemon process environment"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Daemon Service Fast Path Execution\n├── Unix socket connection handler\n│   └── handleConnection() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go:229\n│       └── route to \"run\" method \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go:254\n│           └── handleRun() \u003c-- 7a\n│               ├── parse RunParams from JSON \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go:330\n│               ├── resolve skill manifest \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go:339\n│               ├── buildSkillEnv() \u003c-- 7c\n│               │   ├── add workspace to env \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/daemon/service.go:393\n│               │   └── propagate session vars \u003c-- 7d\n│               │       └── os.Getenv(key) \u003c-- 7e\n│               └── runner.RunWithOptions() \u003c-- 7b\n│                   ├── switch on distribution type \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/runner/runner.go:84\n│                   ├── execrunner.Runner.Run() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/runner/runner.go:93\n│                   │   └── exec.CommandContext() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/exec/exec.go:86\n│                   └── wasirunner.Runner.Run() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/runner/runner.go:102\n│                       └── runtime.InstantiateModule() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/wasi/wasi.go:105",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen agentctl runs skills (executable tools that extend agent capabilities), the typical execution path involves multiple layers: job preparation, state persistence, observability tracking, and cleanup. This adds **~300ms of latency** per skill invocation. For interactive workflows where an AI agent might call dozens of skills in rapid succession, this overhead becomes a significant bottleneck.\n\nThe **daemon service** solves this by providing a **persistent background process** that keeps resources warm (database connections, skill manifests, configuration) and offers a **fast path** that bypasses job orchestration entirely [7a]. Skills execute in **\u003c50ms** instead of 300ms, making agent interactions feel responsive.\n\n## Details\n\n### Architecture\n\nThe daemon runs as a Unix socket server [service.go:229] that accepts JSON-RPC-style requests. When a \"run\" request arrives [service.go:254], it takes the fast path through `handleRun()` [7a].\n\n### Execution Flow\n\n1. **Parse request**: Deserializes `RunParams` containing skill name, input JSON, and optional workspace [service.go:330]\n\n2. **Resolve skill**: Uses a pre-warmed `SkillResolver` to locate the skill manifest and binary without disk I/O overhead [service.go:339]\n\n3. **Build environment**: Constructs environment variables including workspace path and **session tracking variables** [7c]. The daemon propagates `AGENTCTL_SESSION_ID`, `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`, and other session identifiers from its own environment [7d, 7e], enabling skills to maintain lineage across tool invocations.\n\n4. **Execute directly**: Calls `runner.RunWithOptions()` [7b] which routes to either:\n   - **Exec runtime** for native binaries [runner.go:93] → `exec.CommandContext()` [exec.go:86]\n   - **WASI runtime** for WebAssembly modules [runner.go:102] → `runtime.InstantiateModule()` [wasi.go:105]\n\n### Key Optimization\n\nBy calling `RunWithOptions()` directly, the daemon **skips**:\n- Job record creation in SQLite\n- State transitions (queued → running → ok)\n- Result persistence to disk\n- Progress tracking infrastructure\n- Observability event enrichment from cloud metadata\n\nThis makes the daemon ideal for **ephemeral skill calls** where you need the result immediately but don't need durable job history.\n\n### Session Propagation\n\nThe daemon inherits session variables from its parent process and propagates them to child skills [service.go:396-403]. This ensures that skills executed through the daemon can still identify which AI coding session (Claude, Cursor, etc.) triggered them, maintaining proper lineage for debugging and observability."
    },
    {
