        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Platform-Specific Resource Limit Enforcement\n├── Linux Implementation (rlimit_linux.go)\n│   └── setResourceLimits() entry \u003c-- 8a\n│       ├── Initialize SysProcAttr \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/exec/rlimit_linux.go:12\n│       ├── Set process group isolation \u003c-- 8b\n│       ├── Set parent death signal \u003c-- 8c\n│       └── Prepare rlimits (not enforced yet) \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/exec/rlimit_linux.go:23\n│\n└── Unix Implementation (rlimit_unix.go)\n    └── setResourceLimits() entry \u003c-- 8d\n        ├── Initialize SysProcAttr \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/exec/rlimit_unix.go:12\n        └── Set process group isolation \u003c-- 8e\n\nCalled from:\nexec.Runner.Run() \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/exec/exec.go:54\n└── cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, r.Binary) \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/exec/exec.go:86\n    └── setResourceLimits(cmd, maxMemory, maxCPU) \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/execution/exec/exec.go:169\n        ├── Linux: Setpgid + Pdeathsig\n        └── Unix: Setpgid only",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nWhen executing native binary skills as subprocesses, **proper resource isolation is critical** to prevent runaway processes from consuming system resources or persisting after the parent dies. Without process group isolation, killing the parent process leaves orphaned child processes running. Without resource limits, a misbehaving skill can exhaust CPU or memory. The platform-specific resource limit system solves this by applying OS-level process controls during skill execution.\n\nThe challenge is that **different Unix-like systems provide different isolation mechanisms**. Linux offers `Pdeathsig` (parent death signal) to ensure children die with their parent [8c], while macOS and other Unix systems lack this feature. Both support process groups via `Setpgid` for coordinated cleanup [8b, 8e].\n\n## Details\n\n### Architecture\n\nThe exec runner applies resource limits through **platform-specific implementations** using Go's build tags:\n- `rlimit_linux.go` for Linux systems [8a]\n- `rlimit_unix.go` for non-Linux Unix systems (macOS, BSD) [8d]\n- `rlimit_windows.go` for Windows (no-op currently)\n\nBoth implementations are called from the same point in the exec runner's `Run()` method, right before executing the binary [8a, 8d].\n\n### Linux Implementation\n\nOn Linux, `setResourceLimits()` configures two key protections:\n\n1. **Process group isolation** via `cmd.SysProcAttr.Setpgid = true` [8b] - Places the child in its own process group, allowing the entire group to be killed together\n2. **Parent death signal** via `cmd.SysProcAttr.Pdeathsig = syscall.SIGKILL` [8c] - Ensures the child receives SIGKILL if the parent dies unexpectedly\n\nThe function also prepares rlimit structures for memory and CPU limits, but these aren't yet enforceable via the standard library (requires Go 1.23+ or external tools).\n\n### Unix (Non-Linux) Implementation\n\nOn macOS and other Unix systems, `setResourceLimits()` only configures **process group isolation** [8e]. The `Pdeathsig` feature is Linux-specific and unavailable on these platforms. This means Unix systems rely more heavily on context timeouts and explicit cleanup.\n\n### Current Limitations\n\n**Memory and CPU rlimits are documented but not enforced** in the current implementation. The primary enforcement mechanisms are:\n1. Context timeouts (always enforced)\n2. Process group isolation (Unix/Linux)\n3. Parent death signal (Linux only)\n\nFuture versions will leverage Go 1.23+'s `Prlimit` field for proper rlimit enforcement."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Maps the skill execution system with two runtime types (exec for native binaries, WASI for WebAssembly), environment propagation for session tracking across AI tools, and orchestration layers. Key entry points: unified runner [1a], exec runtime [2b], WASI runtime [3c], session env building [4b], job orchestration [5c], hook integration [6c], and daemon service [7b].",
  "mermaidDiagram": "graph TB\n    subgraph Runner[\"Unified Runner\"]\n        1a[\"1a: RunWithOptions\u003cbr/\u003eroutes to runtime\"]\n        1b[\"1b: extract workspace\u003cbr/\u003efrom context\"]\n        1c[\"1c: dispatch by\u003cbr/\u003edistribution type\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph EnvProp[\"Session Environment\"]\n        4a[\"4a: buildSkillEnv\u003cbr/\u003econstructs environment\"]\n        4b[\"4b: iterate session\u003cbr/\u003evariables\"]\n        4c[\"4c: read from parent\u003cbr/\u003eprocess\"]\n        4d[\"4d: propagate to\u003cbr/\u003echild process\"]\n        4e[\"4e: ResolveSessionID\u003cbr/\u003epriority order\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph ExecRuntime[\"Exec Runtime\"]\n        2a[\"2a: Run entry point\u003cbr/\u003enative binary\"]\n        2b[\"2b: create subprocess\u003cbr/\u003ewith context\"]\n        2d[\"2d: inject skill\u003cbr/\u003emetadata\"]\n        2e[\"2e: set command\u003cbr/\u003eenvironment\"]\n        2f[\"2f: apply resource\u003cbr/\u003elimits\"]\n        2g[\"2g: execute binary\u003cbr/\u003eand wait\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph WasiRuntime[\"WASI Runtime\"]\n        3a[\"3a: Run entry point\u003cbr/\u003eWASM module\"]\n        3b[\"3b: initialize wazero\u003cbr/\u003eruntime\"]\n        3c[\"3c: compile WASM\u003cbr/\u003emodule\"]\n        3d[\"3d: build module\u003cbr/\u003econfiguration\"]\n        3e[\"3e: inject environment\u003cbr/\u003evariables\"]\n        3g[\"3g: instantiate and\u003cbr/\u003eexecute module\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph JobExec[\"Job Executor\"]\n        5a[\"5a: RunSkill entry\u003cbr/\u003epoint\"]\n        5b[\"5b: prepare job\u003cbr/\u003erecord\"]\n        5c[\"5c: execute via\u003cbr/\u003eskillExecutor\"]\n        5d[\"5d: update state\u003cbr/\u003eto running\"]\n        5f[\"5f: persist success\u003cbr/\u003estate\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph HookSys[\"Hook System\"]\n        6a[\"6a: Dispatch entry\u003cbr/\u003eroutes events\"]\n        6b[\"6b: execute hook\u003cbr/\u003evia runner\"]\n        6c[\"6c: hook skill\u003cbr/\u003eexecution\"]\n        6d[\"6d: build hook\u003cbr/\u003eenvironment\"]\n        6e[\"6e: propagate session\u003cbr/\u003eto hook\"]\n        6f[\"6f: parse hook\u003cbr/\u003eoutput\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph DaemonSvc[\"Daemon Service\"]\n        7a[\"7a: handleRun\u003cbr/\u003evia socket\"]\n        7b[\"7b: execute via\u003cbr/\u003eunified runner\"]\n        7c[\"7c: build daemon\u003cbr/\u003eenvironment\"]\n        7d[\"7d: propagate session\u003cbr/\u003evars\"]\n    end\n    \n    subgraph ResLimits[\"Resource Limits\"]\n        8a[\"8a: Linux limits\u003cbr/\u003ewith Pdeathsig\"]\n        8b[\"8b: set process\u003cbr/\u003egroup isolation\"]\n        8c[\"8c: parent death\u003cbr/\u003esignal\"]\n        8d[\"8d: Unix limits\u003cbr/\u003ebasic isolation\"]\n        8e[\"8e: Unix process\u003cbr/\u003egroup\"]\n    end\n    \n    1b --\u003e|extracts| 1a\n    1c --\u003e|routes| 1a\n    \n    1a --\u003e|calls for exec| 4a\n    1a --\u003e|calls for WASI| 4a\n    4a --\u003e|reads| 4b\n    4b --\u003e|gets value| 4c\n    4c --\u003e|adds to env| 4d\n    4a --\u003e|resolves| 4e\n    \n    4a --\u003e|provides env| 2a\n    1a --\u003e|creates exec runner| 2b\n    2b --\u003e|uses| 2d\n    2d --\u003e|sets| 2e\n    2e --\u003e|applies| 2f\n    2f --\u003e|enforces| 8a\n    2f --\u003e|enforces| 8d\n    2e --\u003e|runs| 2g\n    \n    4a --\u003e|provides env| 3a\n    1a --\u003e|creates WASI runner| 3b\n    3b --\u003e|compiles| 3c\n    3c --\u003e|configures| 3d\n    3d --\u003e|injects| 3e\n    3e --\u003e|executes| 3g\n    \n    5a --\u003e|prepares| 5b\n    5b --\u003e|executes| 5c\n    5c --\u003e|calls| 1a\n    5c --\u003e|updates| 5d\n    5c --\u003e|persists| 5f\n    \n    6a --\u003e|routes| 6b\n    6b --\u003e|executes| 6c\n    6c --\u003e|calls| 1a\n    6c --\u003e|builds| 6d\n    6d --\u003e|propagates| 6e\n    6c --\u003e|parses| 6f\n    \n    7a --\u003e|handles| 7b\n    